Title: THE SUMMIT NOTE
Author: Alex Rivera
Draft date: June 2026

FADE IN:


EXT. KATHMANDU - ESTABLISHING - DAY

Gear shops. Permits stamped. A expedition assembles.

EXT. NEPAL BASE CAMP - DAY

JUNE OKAFOR and guide TENZIN review the route. WAX-SEALED ENVELOPE in June's pocket.
TENZIN
Summit window closes in thirty-six hours.

EXT. KHUMBU GLACIER - DAY

Loads carried. Ropes fixed. June lags, reading the envelope again.

EXT. ICE FALL - DAY

Cairn with tin box — M. OKAFOR, 1987.
JUNE
He turned back fifty meters below the ridge.

INT. TENT - NIGHT

Father's coordinates, cave sketch, unfinished sentences.
JUNE
He wasn't quitting. He was hiding something.

EXT. HIGH CAMP - NIGHT

Storm rolls early. Tenzin wants descent. June argues for one push.
TENZIN
The mountain doesn't care about your family.

EXT. SUMMIT APPROACH - DAWN

Wind drops — brief gift. They climb toward the fissure, not the ceremonial summit.

INT. ICE CAVE - DAY

Survey crates. 1985 British labels. Journal with June's father's name.
JUNE
They measured the peak wrong by sixty meters. He wouldn't lie on a map.

EXT. SUMMIT RIDGE - DAY

Tensing watches the weather clock. June copies the journal's final page.
TENZIN
We leave now with proof, or we leave forever without it.

EXT. DESCENT TRAIL - DUSK

June descends with the journal photographed, envelope burned for warmth. Behind her, the true summit gleams — forty meters higher than history says.
JUNE
Next season, we put his name on the right line.

FADE OUT.


THE END
